WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.300
B

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.868
-We're back with
Kenan Thompson.

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.737
Now, this is not the only book
you've written this year.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.539
You also have done some writing
under a pen name.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.975
-Yes, I have a pen name
that I like to write under.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.611
-You've been doing
some science fiction work?

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:15.048
-That's right, I introduced
it here for the first time,

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:18.317
the actual fact that I am
the one and only Pernice.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:21.087
So, yeah, if I could, um...

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.588
-Do you want to...
Would it be helpful?

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.924
I would love to talk to Pernice.
And would you want to leave?

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.493
-He's been writing more
and more and more.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.860
And there's a new book
that he wrote

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.295
that he would like to present.

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:30.964
-Alright. So, well, why don't
you leave, Kenan,

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.732
and then we'll bring out
Pernice Lafonk.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.567
-Yeah, I'm gonna, 'cause
we're two different people.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:35.935
-Of course.
-Know what I mean?

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.271
So I'm gonna go.
and then Pernice will appear.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.572
So that'll be that.
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.107
-And I want to make it clear --

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.642
your team, as you call them,

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.410
has made it very clear to me
when you're out,

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.979
I should only refer
to you as Pernice.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.379
-It would be nice.
Yes, it would be nice.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:48.848
Yeah. Thank you very much.

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:50.783
-Okay. So why don't you go
and I'll give...

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.118
-I'll go now.
-Okay, great.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:54.253
-I'll go now. Alright.
Just coming back.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.489
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:02.428
-Our next guest is a gifted
science fiction writer

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:06.166
who you know from his
bestseller "Quinsley's Nebula,"

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.801
part of his wildly popular
Quark series.

00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:11.103
Here to talk about his
highly anticipated follow-up,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.440
please welcome back
to the show Pernice Lafonk.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.609
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:24.750 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:31.491 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:35.194
Pernice, what an honor
to have you back,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.595
back on the show.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:40.065
-It is a pleasure to see you
as well, Seth Meyers.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:43.569
-Now, Pernice, I hear --
you know, I have connections,

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.839
contacts in
the literary sphere --

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:50.076
that you're dabbling in a new
genre called space erotica.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.877
-Yes.
-Would you -- would you do us

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:53.613
an honor of reading
an excerpt from your latest?

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.948
And what is this one?
I'll hand you a copy here.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.185
What is this one called?
-Uh, this is my latest work,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.887
called
"Amazon Boobies on the Moon."

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.889
-Uh-huh. Right.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.358
-You like that title, Sethly?

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.494
-I do, I do.
I enjoy that title a great deal.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.831
-Have I dipped my ink slightly
into erotica with this one?

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.300
Perhaps just the tip.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.302
Uh, but you tell me, Seth.
Here we go.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.638
-Oh, this is the reading.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.607
"Amazon Boobies on the Moon"
by Pernice Lafonk.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:25.878
-We'll start with
chapter eight, naturally.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:29.214
Chapter eight, beta three.

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.050
"Tokyo. Tokyo.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.885
Tune in, Tokyo.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.221
Tokyo. Toronto.

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.223
Tunisia.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.028
Nada. Radio silence.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.029
The sounds of nothingness
echoed through

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.532
his not-so-trusty spacecraft,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.568
the Perineum Falcon.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:55.908
'Drab nabbit!' Lieutenant
Val Deferens bellowed.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:59.879
'The comms seem to be
malfunctioning again.'

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:03.449
And then a series of gasps.
Hup, hup!

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:07.119
Taking shallow breaths,
he became panic stricken

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.354
as he watched
his oxygen levels drop.

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:13.559
Drop slowly, sensually,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:17.197
like a loose spaghetti-strap
brassiere

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.399
at the end
of a tough day at the office."

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.835
Oh, this is good.
This is good stuff.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:26.105
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:29.242
"Val's mind raced with thoughts
of Bernadette

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:30.910
and immediate regret.

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:34.213
If only he hadn't squandered
the last of his lunar credits

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.916
on the latest issue
of 'Pernthouse.'

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:40.486
And what had become
of the promise

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.821
that ne'er 'twould he
find himself

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.556
in such a treacherous pickle.

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:47.926
Penniless, surrounded
by alien dangerosity.

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:51.430
Nevertheless, it can get
rather lonely

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.466
in the deep, dark depths
of the universe.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:58.104
With one final 'ga-gonk,'

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:01.573
Lieutenant Val Deferens
spanked the control 'pernel'

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.041
with all of his might."

00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:06.712
-Pernel?
-Pernel. Yes.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.716
-"All of a sudden -- ka-toosh!

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.217
Ba-bussy!"

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.218
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:16.389
"The Perineum Falcon's engines
roared back to life

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.690
with an electrical emission

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:20.426
that registered a double-D
on the dashboard."

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.661
-Wow. I mean...

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:25.164
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.834
-It's good.
-Really.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.168
There you are.
That proves you wrote it.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.437
It proves you wrote it.
I mean, that...

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:32.971
-My proof.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.940
-Not only does that tick

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:36.909
every box I need
for good science fiction,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.712
that's also everything
I want out of my erotica.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.147
-Well, thank you very much.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.648
Thank you very much.
-I could tell...

00:04:42.714 --> 00:04:44.416
I hope you don't mind me
saying,

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:47.420
I feel as though you were also

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:50.790
maybe a little turned on
by your own writing.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:54.493
-Oh, I keep
a constant erection as I'm --

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.796
as I'm -- as I'm sitting
at my typewriter.

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:59.498
It's a must be the sound
of the clicks.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.899
-You have one of those
standing desks?

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.135
-I stand at the desk
and I am just full out there,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.237
and just ready at any moment.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:06.572
-Yeah.
-Ready at any moment.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.140
-You know,
one of the telltale signs

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.476
of arousal, as well, is when
someone's a sideburns flip out.

00:05:11.543 --> 00:05:14.380
-Yeah, that's a thing.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.849
When you're really,
really excited,

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.852
your sideburns tend to flare.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.120
-And that's what's happening
now, as you can see.

00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:23.689
-Well, Publishers Weekly
said about this book --

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.625
"It's a real sideburn flarer."
-Yep. That's right.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.460
I think that's on the back,
actually.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:29.962
Publishers -- Yeah.
"Sideburn flarer."

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.330
-Oh, my God. Well, Pernice...
-Thank you.

00:05:31.396 --> 00:05:33.532
-We do -- would love you
to promise

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.367
to keep coming back and sharing
your new writing with us.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.870
-I shall, I shall. I wonder
where the next one will be.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.405
Maybe in the desert.
-Ooh!

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.739
-What would that be called?
-Well, I love

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:42.174
watching your mind work
in real time.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.410
-Right? Maybe the desert.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.745
We'll write about the desert,
and scorpions.

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:49.715
Yes. Scorpions, the sting.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.617
Ah, I love it.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:54.754
-Oh, my God, you guys.
That's Pernice Lafonk.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.822
A.k.a. Kenan Thompson.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.391
"SNL" returns this week --

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.559
Dakota Johnson,
Justin Timberlake.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.261
We'll be right back
with Ronny Chieng.

